WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:09.840
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:20.370
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.910
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.560
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:07.040
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:14.310
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:21.050
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:28.480
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.180
Dominüra?

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.320
You said you’d
do it for me, right?

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.740
The Emerald Ri Majon.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.750
The Simouns are the
vehicles of the gods.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:47.960
They can’t fall.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.200
But that’s…

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.960
…the Emerald Ri Majon!

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:05.930
<b>The Ruins</b>

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.640
Hey, check that out
for me, will you?

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.380
Adjust the oil pressure for
the communication-wire ejectors!

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.980
I need somebody to
pull on this for me!

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.610
So we’re going to be
working here again.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:53.650
Yes.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.520
First off, I want you all
to thoroughly pinpoint…

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.540
…the areas that sustained damage.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.990
Right! We’re already on it!

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.490
How is the old place?

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.000
Sibylla…

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.250
You look well. Glad to see it.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.870
Yes.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:17.920
Likewise.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.940
We just got back, and things
are already hectic, I see.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:26.150
Yes, we were told to put a
rush on the Simoun repairs.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:27.260
Hmm.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:32.320
Um.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.230
Huh?

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:34.480
Excuse me.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.190
I need you to take
a look at the lift.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.230
Fine.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.240
Sibylla.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.280
Please excuse me.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.400
All right.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.000
Now that Shoukoku and the
highlands have formed an alliance…

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:00.160
…it’s only a matter of
time before they attack.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:06.490
Meaning we’ll have to ask the sibyllae
again to carry out such a cruel task.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.260
It’s not a request.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.340
It’s an order, Guragief.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.950
All of this happened
because of me.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.990
All because of
my own selfishness!

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:27.530
To think that I could ever forget
Amuria and the Emerald Ri Majon…

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.540
How could you have
been so naïve, Neviril?

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:54.850
There are so many things that
must never be forgotten, Neviril!

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.540
Dominüra and Rimone…

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.750
They vanished, didn’t they?

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.430
The Emerald Ri Majon…

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.260
…failed, I suppose.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:39.100
Or maybe what really happened
was that they copped out!

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:42.730
If that were true, it would at
least offer some consolation.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:47.640
No. What matters is not
the cause but the result.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:51.780
For once again, we have lost
precious comrades of ours.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.300
We’ve come home to the
Arcus Prima, haven’t we?

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.930
How can you be so
cavalier about this, Floe?

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:11.640
Then are you saying that you’re
not glad to be back, Alty?

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.930
Of course I’m glad!

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.770
Sure I’m glad, but still…

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.600
Come on, we’re going to
be roommates, you know.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.210
Let’s try to get along.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:24.340
I guess you’re right.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.830
Welcome back, everyone…

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.200
…to the Arcus Prima!

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:53.220
I know that you have all gone through
many changes during this time…

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.110
…and we are most…

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.810
The center was destroyed in the attack.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:01.200
As for the 12 Simouns belonging
to Chor Rubor and Chor Caput…

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.630
…we had no choice but to abandon
any hopes of restoring them.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:04.730
At this time…

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.570
…the only chor remaining
on the Arcus Prima…

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.070
…is your own, Chor Tempest.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.030
High Priestess.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.580
What has become of the members
of Chor Rubor and Chor Caput?

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.750
Nearly all of the sibyllae
have gone to the Spring.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.670
You mean you gave them the axe.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.660
Watch your mouth, Aer!

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.670
Come on, you know it’s true!

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.390
If there are no Simouns
to fly, they don’t need us.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:27.420
Silence!

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:38.310
Now then, there’s somebody here
who would like to meet with you all.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:45.960
Father!

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.950
Welcome home, Neviril.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.300
I have returned, Father.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:06.060
That goes for all of you
Chor Tempest sibyllae.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.090
We are happy that you
made it back safely.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.980
Father.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.340
Oh, that’s right.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.680
Yes, I know.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:18.550
Sibylla Rimone and Sibylla
Dominüra are no longer with us.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.100
That’s right.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.810
We are now headed toward the Ruins.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.310
The Ruins?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.270
Why the Ruins?

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.070
We all know it’s
no simple matter to…

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.030
You are correct, Sibylla Yun.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:37.640
The Ruins happen to be the holiest
place in all of Simulacrum Kyuukoku.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:39.990
Not to mention a forbidden area.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.060
However, it is imperative that…

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:48.040
…we reach the Ruins before the
forces of Shoukoku and the highlands.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.050
By any chance…

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:02.370
Yes, what is your
question, Sibylla Floe?

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.810
By any chance, are you forcing us?

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.860
The only ones in all of
Simulacrum Kyuukoku…

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.900
…who have the ability
to execute this strategy…

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.820
This is not a request.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:20.780
You are all expected to participate
in this battle without exception.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:25.540
I guess this means we don’t have the
right to go to the Spring anymore.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.290
Yes.

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.550
Most likely…

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:33.050
…we have nowhere to escape to.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.260
The only thing we
can do is move on.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:34.270
I never thought I’d get the opportunity
to speak with you like this again.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:35.320
No.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.310
Neviril is no longer
the daughter I knew…

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:40.750
…who would do anything I’d ask of her.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:45.200
And so there is nothing
more I can do for you.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.250
Oh, no. I am grateful that you took
me under your wing, Vice Chancellor.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.350
What?

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:54.520
No…

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.170
It’s just that you seem
to be a changed person.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.350
Yes.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:26.430
We owe you our lives.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:30.510
If it hadn’t been for the Arcus Prima,
the Messis would have surely fallen.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.370
You have done well.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.060
Thank goodness we were in time.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.500
But still, Captain…

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.550
Yes?

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:42.720
You entrusted me with 12 sibyllae,
and I failed to return them all to you.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.050
Please forgive me.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.470
Captain Wauf.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.680
Yes?

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.130
A detailed report can wait.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:51.690
In your opinion…

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.310
…are Sibylla Dominüra
and Sibylla Rimone…

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.770
I believe that they are both alive.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.710
Then what exactly happened to them?

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:04.360
That I don’t know. However…

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:09.370
Perhaps we will find the answer
to that question at the Ruins.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.350
Neviril!

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.520
Aer, quickly!

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:35.980
Right!

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.070
— Neviril.
— What is it?

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.700
Oh… nothing.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:46.330
Para-sama! Hurry!

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.810
I know this is hardest on you.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:18.890
No.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:22.440
I’m not the one who
has to suffer the most.

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:02.830
Look.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:11.960
As planned…

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:14.620
…with communication cables
intact, Chor Tempest…

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.800
…will descend as low as possible…

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:21.380
…and protect the Ruins from attack
by the Shoukoku-highland forces.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:57.870
So these are the Ruins.

00:14:58.490 --> 00:14:59.620
Yes.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.370
This is my first time here as well.

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:04.880
This is Tempus Spatium’s holy land.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:07.630
I don’t think the enemy
is here yet, do you?

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:09.340
Don’t let your guard down!

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.220
Oh, don’t be so bossy!

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:12.680
Two o’clock!

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.230
What’s that?

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:25.360
Could those be Simouns?

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.320
But I’ve never seen
anything like them before!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.360
Nor have I!

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:33.370
What should we do, Para-sama?

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.490
Para-sama!

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:37.370
Go after them!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.240
Yes!

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:43.250
We’ll take the one on the left!

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.580
Leave it to me!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.390
Are they planning to attack?

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.650
The Shark Ri Majon?

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:08.860
No way!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.230
The enemy?

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:18.020
Hurry, go after them, Para-sama!
We can’t let them get away!

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:20.830
Who are they? Who’s
operating those Simouns?

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:23.830
Who’s flying those Simouns
to pray to the skies?

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:25.910
You’re right.

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:28.590
How can they
possibly fly like that?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.440
Enemies… Is that the enemy?

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:38.010
I won’t let them get away!

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.560
They’re firing at us!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:41.980
I’m not afraid!

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:47.730
B-But, how could those
Simouns be enemies of ours?

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.520
Let’s worry about that later, Floe!

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.530
Aer?

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:57.790
Aer, what do you
think you’re doing?

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:58.940
Hurry!

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.450
Aer!

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:05.100
Leave the pursuit to the others.
Let’s see what’s inside those Ruins.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.130
What?

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.590
What on earth are
you talking about?

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:09.790
My music box…

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.180
…it’s playing now.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:15.960
It’s closed, but
it’s still playing!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:17.830
What?

00:17:46.760 --> 00:17:48.090
They managed to get away.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.790
What should we do now, Para-sama?

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.300
Head back to the Ruins.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:00.100
Hey, it stopped.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:02.890
Come on, let’s go, Aer.

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.310
H-Hey…

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:05.730
Hold on a minute!

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:08.410
How come you’re acting
like this all of a sudden?

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.410
But this is…

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.820
What’s the matter, Neviril?

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.580
They think they’re gonna get away!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.700
Not if I have my way!

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.840
Huh? What the…

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:36.700
The Spring.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.950
I hit it.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.620
Just one down after all that?

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:17.680
Onasia!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.450
Onasia…

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:23.980
I am glad that you’re here…

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:25.990
…Sibylla Neviril…

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.140
…Sibylla Aer…

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:29.800
But why…

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.400
…why are you here, Onasia?

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.670
Sibylla Neviril…

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.820
…I happen to be everywhere.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:40.900
And yet nowhere.

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:45.470
Can’t catch up…

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.120
Who in the world
is flying that thing?

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.950
Good question.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.620
And besides, there’s something
not right about this place.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:53.630
Let’s go back!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.130
Yes!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.480
Onasia, how can…

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:14.650
…this place be exactly
the same as the Spring?

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.910
Tempus watches over
the flow of time.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.640
While Spatium shows us
mankind’s rightful place.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.660
And when these two become a pair…

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:29.650
…they bestow boundless
blessings and fear to the people.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.260
Yun?

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:43.800
Huh?

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:44.880
A Simoun?

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:58.920
Yun!

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:01.380
Yun, what’s wrong?

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:06.890
This place… What exactly
is going on in this place?

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:12.580
Yun!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.620
Yun!

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:15.490
Here in the Ruins…

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:18.600
…time and space…

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:24.090
…are released from all curses.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.560
Hold on a second, Yun.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:41.360
Just what was going on back there?

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:42.980
They’re all…

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.200
…waiting for me.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:47.790
Neviril.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.630
I know what’s going on.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:52.410
This isn’t just some place
that looks like the Spring.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:54.250
What?

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:55.870
What do you mean, Aer?

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:58.080
This place is…

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.040
…the Spring itself.

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:02.620
It’s just like Grandpa said!

00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:19.230
Anglas!

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:30.110
Aer!

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:47.900
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:52.140
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:59.210
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.210 --> 00:23:06.810
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:19.700
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:24.870
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:28.850
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:32.890
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:38.750
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:44.300
<i>Soar away into the
sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:47.730
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:53.400
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:59.630
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.670
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:12.720
Aer and Mamina have been barred
from attending Anglas’s funeral.

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:15.550
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:20.020
<b>The Funeral</b>

00:24:16.970 --> 00:24:18.320
The Funeral.
